1
00:00:01,571 --> 00:00:11,967
FinSight 2.0 — the executive cloud intelligence layer. Ask your cloud estate a question in plain English and get a grounded, cited answer.

2
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:29,289
Under the hood, two deterministic engines own every number. Capacity-Mngt-App forecasts utilisation and spend; Cost-Mngt-App detects anomalies and attributes cost. Their outputs become fact cards, and the RAG layer can only cite those facts.

3
00:00:29,289 --> 00:00:43,691
The executive cockpit: one screen, three engines' worth of signal.

4
00:00:43,691 --> 00:01:00,542
KPI strip: ~$4.97M annualized spend · 51 anomalies · 1 CRITICAL capacity stream

5
00:01:00,542 --> 00:01:12,993
Capacity-Mngt-App: worst-first. Assist / us-east-1 is already over the 80% headroom line.

6
00:01:12,993 --> 00:01:28,103
Cost-Mngt-App: spikes scored by robust z (median + MAD) — hover a row for the root cause.

7
00:01:28,103 --> 00:01:39,323
45-day spend forecast with a 95% prediction interval — in-sample MAPE ≈ 1.2%.

8
00:01:39,323 --> 00:01:44,484
Now the point of FinSight: just ask.

9
00:01:44,484 --> 00:02:01,948
Q1 — forward risk. Answer leads with the CRITICAL stream and cites [FACT-012].

10
00:02:01,948 --> 00:02:14,492
Q2 — backward look. Spike, baseline, z-score and suspected cause — all cited.

11
00:02:14,492 --> 00:02:28,534
Q3 — drill-down. Naming a region + service boosts exact-match facts.

12
00:02:28,534 --> 00:02:40,509
Q4 — a health check on one stream: capacity and cost evidence together.

13
00:02:40,509 --> 00:02:55,468
Q5 — off-domain. No evidence, no answer. FinSight declines instead of hallucinating.

14
00:02:55,468 --> 00:03:08,581
Everything here is also an API. The same grounded answers, citations and evidence are one POST away, so FinSight can sit behind Slack, Teams, or an agent.

15
00:03:08,581 --> 00:03:21,740
FinSight 2.0: deterministic engines own the numbers, the language model only phrases them. Runs offline in template mode, or fluent with Claude — one command to demo.

